%9Setting:%9

    nick_mode_color_owner, nick_mode_color_op, nick_mode_color_halfop,
    nick_mode_color_voice, nick_mode_color_normal (strings)

%9Description:%9

    Colours the mode prefix that $nickmode puts before a nick.

    Operators and voiced users stand out. There is one setting for each rank:

        nick_mode_color_owner     owner, ~ or &
        nick_mode_color_op        op, @
        nick_mode_color_halfop    halfop, %%
        nick_mode_color_voice     voice, +
        nick_mode_color_normal    no mode (the blank that $nickmode prints)

    Each value is a format code, for example %%Y%%_ or %%ZF59E0B%%_ (24-bit
    colour F59E0B, bold). An empty value leaves the prefix uncoloured, which
    is the default of all five. The Shellter default configuration sets:

        nick_mode_color_owner     %%ZFF7B72%%_
        nick_mode_color_op        %%ZF59E0B%%_
        nick_mode_color_halfop    %%Z3FB950%%_
        nick_mode_color_voice     %%Z79C0FF%%_

    nick_mode_color_normal stays empty there.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET nick_mode_color_op %%ZF59E0B%%_
    /SET nick_mode_color_voice %%C
    /SET -clear nick_mode_color_op

%9See also:%9

    SET, NICKMODE, NICK_MODE_COLOR_OWNER, NICK_MODE_COLOR_OP,
    NICK_MODE_COLOR_HALFOP, NICK_MODE_COLOR_VOICE, NICK_MODE_COLOR_NORMAL
